course: dictionary
lesson: 835
title: Beneath: under, and not good enough
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Beneath means under or below something. Look at the clues: «Rivers can be deep and fast just beneath a calm surface.» The river looks calm on top, but the deep, fast water is under it. Swap in under and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: «Beech trees make a thick roof of leaves, so little grows beneath them.» The roof of leaves is above, and the plants are below it. Beneath is a more literary word for under, so you will often meet it in stories and poems.
explain: Beneath has a second meaning, about people. If something is beneath someone, it is not good enough for them, or too low for them to do. This is often used in a proud or rude way, so look at the feeling in the sentence before you decide what it means.
fact: Beneath means under or below something.
fact: Beneath is a preposition when it comes before a noun, as in «beneath the surface» or «beneath the soil».
fact: Beneath can also be an adverb, used on its own to mean below or underneath, with no noun after it.
fact: Beneath someone means not good enough for them, or too low for them to do, and is often used in a proud or rude way.
fact: Useful phrases: beneath the surface means hidden under the top layer; beneath you means too low for you to do.
exercise: «Little grows beneath the beech trees, except bluebells.» What does beneath mean here? | Above the top | *Under or below | Beside, next to | Inside a box
exercise: Ruby says, «That job is beneath me.» What does she mean? | She is very short | It is at the bottom of the hill | She wants the job more than anyone | *It is not good enough for her to do
exercise: Which word means the same as beneath? | bright | above | quickly | *under
test: In «the curved ground falls away beneath it», where is the ground compared with the satellite? | Above the satellite | Beside the satellite | Inside the satellite | *Below the satellite
test: Which sentence uses beneath to mean not good enough for someone? | Little grows beneath the trees | Roots spread beneath the soil | *He said the chore was beneath him | The rock lay beneath the sea
exam: What does «just beneath a calm surface» tell us about the river? | It is frozen solid | It is dry and empty | *Fast, deep water hidden under the calm top | It flows uphill
